WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:05.355
Many people had led armies against the Yellow Turbans.

2
00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:09.144
Most of them received government jobs.

3
00:00:09.145 --> 00:00:14.874
Dong Zhuo became Emperor Ling's top advisor.

4
00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:19.457
Officials in the imperial court were reviewing documents.

5
00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:27.425
"Hmm," one said. "This report says Liu Bei helped Dong Zhuo at the battle of Guangzong.

6
00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.957
So, why wasn't he given a government job?"

7
00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:36.178
"Oh, I know all about that," another official said.

8
00:00:36.179 --> 00:00:42.647
"Dong Zhuo refused to admit Liu Bei helped him." He shrugged.

9
00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:46.040
"So, Liu Bei didn't get a fancy job."

10
00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:54.501
The first official groaned. "We shouldn't make decisions based on one general's feelings.

11
00:00:54.502 --> 00:00:59.311
Corruption like that caused the Yellow Turban Rebellion in the first place!"

12
00:00:59.312 --> 00:01:12.666
"You're right." The other official sighed. "Let's talk to our supervisor."

13
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:16.319
The supervisor agreed with the officials.

14
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.499
He made Liu Bei the magistrate of Anxi County.

15
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.988
The region had a big problem with crime.

16
00:01:24.989 --> 00:01:29.577
As magistrate, Liu Bei would have to deal with that.

17
00:01:29.578 --> 00:01:35.791
Liu Bei brought his oath brothers to Anxi County with him.

18
00:01:35.792 --> 00:01:41.916
"This place stinks!" Zhang Fei said as they moved into their new place.

19
00:01:41.917 --> 00:01:48.278
Guan Yu shrugged. "It's not so bad."

20
00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:51.567
"We'll make it better," Liu Bei said.

21
00:01:51.568 --> 00:01:54.928
A fight broke out in the street.

22
00:01:54.929 --> 00:01:58.166
The brothers hurried outside.

23
00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:01.582
"What's going on?" Liu Bei asked.

24
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:09.412
One man pointed at the other. "He stole my rice. He belongs in prison!"

25
00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:18.332
The other man fell to his knees. "Put me in prison. At least then I won't starve."

26
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:22.645
Liu Bei frowned. "Stand up."

27
00:02:22.646 --> 00:02:25.989
The man climbed back to his feet.

28
00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.500
"Stealing is wrong," Liu Bei said.

29
00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:37.332
"But you're so hungry, you wish to go to prison. That's wrong too.

30
00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:40.999
Nobody should have to go to prison just to eat."

31
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.249
The man scratched his head. "I don't understand."

32
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.743
Liu Bei addressed the people gathered nearby.

33
00:02:49.744 --> 00:02:53.717
"Who will give this man a job and make sure he eats today?"

34
00:02:53.718 --> 00:02:57.053
The man's jaw dropped.

35
00:02:57.054 --> 00:03:01.332
When nobody answered, Guan Yu stepped forward.

36
00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:04.666
"If he steals from you, we'll punish him."

37
00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:10.001
"And I'll pay you back with my own money!" Zhang Fei added.

38
00:03:10.002 --> 00:03:13.838
At that, an old man came forward.

39
00:03:13.839 --> 00:03:20.478
"I need help in my basket shop. I've been searching for an apprentice."

40
00:03:20.479 --> 00:03:24.437
Liu Bei turned to the thief. "Well?"

41
00:03:24.438 --> 00:03:30.285
The man bowed. "I would be honored to learn that skill."

42
00:03:30.286 --> 00:03:34.210
Liu Bei turned to the man whose rice had been stolen.

43
00:03:34.211 --> 00:03:36.696
"Does this seem fair to you?"

44
00:03:36.697 --> 00:03:42.852
The man bowed. "Yes. I don't want anyone to starve."

45
00:03:42.853 --> 00:03:49.500
The people murmured. Everyone admired how fair and just Liu Bei was.

46
00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:57.499
Crime in Anxi County soon vanished.

47
00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:02.832
One day a government inspector visited Liu Bei.

48
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:10.624
The inspector saw the empty prison cells. "Where are the prisoners?"

49
00:04:10.625 --> 00:04:15.259
Liu Bei smiled. "We don't have any."

50
00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:21.205
"Ah, I see." The inspector grinned.

51
00:04:21.206 --> 00:04:25.249
"People bribe you, and you let them go."

52
00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:29.686
Liu Bei was offended. "I would never—"

53
00:04:29.687 --> 00:04:32.244
The inspector held up a hand.

54
00:04:32.245 --> 00:04:36.583
"Of course not! Bribes are illegal."

55
00:04:36.584 --> 00:04:42.739
He grinned, winking at Liu Bei. "You must be rich."

56
00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.764
Liu Bei shook his head. "I'm quite poor actually."

57
00:04:47.765 --> 00:04:54.791
The inspector didn't seem to hear him. "You will need to pay a fee, of course."

58
00:04:54.792 --> 00:05:01.319
"A fee?" Liu Bei raised an eyebrow.

59
00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.493
"You wish to remain magistrate, correct?"

60
00:05:04.494 --> 00:05:07.582
The inspector didn't wait for an answer.

61
00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:13.582
"Then you must pay me—um, I mean, the government."

62
00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:18.858
Liu Bei had no money to pay this corrupt inspector.

63
00:05:18.859 --> 00:05:23.829
He had him thrown out and soon received a letter.

64
00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:36.708
It informed him he was no longer the magistrate of Anxi County.
